From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ryan Murray <address-in-upstream-commit@localhost>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 22:55:53 +1100
Subject: [PATCH 30/37] arm64: dts: apple: t6050: describe the AOP on every
 MacBook Pro

The AOP, with its ambient light and lid angle services and the
microphone array its audio service captures, was enabled only on the
J714s, K114c and K116s. The ADTs of all eight T6050 MacBook Pros (J714c,
J714s, J716c, J716s, K114c, K114s, K116c, K116s) have the same AOP,
setup port, dart-aop, admac-base-ns, ALS, audio service and microphone
array nodes (three microphones on leap-s RX0 through the proxy ADMAC),
with the same addresses, interrupts and DART streams. Only the chassis
name the microphone card takes its identity from differs.

Move the enables and the audio service's DMA channels into a new
t6050-aop.dtsi and include it from all eight boards. Each board sets
only apple,chassis-name: J714 (J714c, J714s), J716 (J716c, J716s), K114
(K114c, K114s) and K116 (K116c, K116s). Values are from each board's
ADT. The J714s, K114c and K116s DTBs are byte-identical; the J775c,
J775d and J873s are unchanged.

The J714s block is DjDeveloperr's, the K114c one Joshua Warren's and the
K116s one Jens Axboe's.

Signed-off-by: Ryan Murray <address-in-upstream-commit@localhost>

[Not carried over: the t6050-k114s.dts hunk of the original. The shared AOP file gives
aop_audio the spkr and sense DMA channels, which the K114s sound card must not have.]

[re-cut onto the K114s r3d tree]
